{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Landed as Gerrit change 3099, commit ed501817343, LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with no advisories. Root cause recorded in the description: 15 shell launches use the literal /bin/sh, which Windows resolves as drive-relative \\bin\\sh (WinError 2 in Windows sweep run 35572919806). The guard is a module-level skipif on /bin/sh being executable. A scratch copy pointed at a nonexistent path reported 15 skipped with the reason; on this host all 15 pass. make verify locally: only the 17 known pandoc failures under tests/unit/reconciler. The Windows sweep effect is tracked in the linked P4 task."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792836648013341001,"uuid":"34e74534-1106-4256-b073-eb0450302ad3"}